    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d770-a2">

                <pb facs="0876" n="796" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg796"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Clayton to Mr.
                            Russell.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Embassy of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-07-29"><hi rendition="#italic">July 29,
                        1901</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    communication of the 25th instant and its inclosure, and to express my
                    appreciation of the thanks of the board of directors of the El Paso Chamber of
                    Commerce.</p>
                <pb facs="0877" n="797" xml:id="pg797"/>
                <p>My report was based upon the best information I could obtain, and I shall be
                    glad, if any errors are made plain to me, to correct the same, or to receive any
                    additional information that may be sent me through any reliable source. I
                    understand an article has been lately published concerning the Hay
                    correspondence in relation to the matter. If you will kindly send me a copy of
                    same you will oblige.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully, yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Powell Clayton.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
